            <ArticleTitle>Atheroembolic perioperative infarction during repeat coronary bypass surgery: angiographic documentation in a survivor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>218-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a patient in whom a myocardial infarction complicated a coronary bypass reoperation. We believe the infarction was associated with embolic occlusion of a large coronary branch by atheroma, which we demonstrated in a previous bypass graft preoperatively and did not see in the postoperative study. We are not aware that atheroembolism of a large coronary branch has been reported before in a survivor of reoperation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
